The GPU user client starts on a machine with no GPU

HakiosGPUUserClient::start() refused unless hakios_gpu_ready(), which is false without
the Adreno GPU. But the selector that has to work without one is kHakiosShow: it
copies pixels into the boot framebuffer and touches no GPU. The dispatch already
answers kIOReturnNotReady to every other selector on such a machine, so the check in
start() only made the panel unpaintable -- which is exactly what it did.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/hakios.gpu.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/hakios.gpu.cpp
@@ HakiosGPUUserClient::start(IOService * provider)
-	if (!hakios_gpu_ready() || !IOUserClient::start(provider)) {
+	/* No GPU is required to open this client: the one selector that must work without
+	 * one is kHakiosShow, which copies pixels into the boot framebuffer and never touches
+	 * a GPU. The dispatch below already answers kIOReturnNotReady to every other selector
+	 * on such a machine, so refusing here only kept the panel unpaintable. */
+	if (!IOUserClient::start(provider)) {
 		return false;
 	}
